.TH "SLIPWAY-API-RESOURCES" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-api\-resources \- Print the supported resource types
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway api\-resources"
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the supported resource types.
.PP
Prints a table of the resource types slipway knows, sorted by name. A command accepts a type by its NAME, its singular or one of its SHORTNAMES. Type words are case\-insensitive. Use \-o wide to add the verbs that act on each type, and \-o name to print only the names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. One of: table, wide, name. (default "table")
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
When using the default output format, don't print headers.
.SH COLUMNS
Every type shows NAME, SHORTNAMES, KIND and GROUPED, and \-o wide adds VERBS. A type without aliases reads <none> in SHORTNAMES.
.TP
\fBNAME\fR
The name of the type, in the plural.
.TP
\fBSHORTNAMES\fR
The aliases of the type, besides its singular.
.TP
\fBKIND\fR
The kind a manifest of the type declares.
.TP
\fBGROUPED\fR
Whether resources of the type live in a group, so that \-n and \-A scope them. kubectl's NAMESPACED column says the same about namespaces.
.TP
\fBVERBS\fR
The commands that act on resources of the type.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Print the supported resource types
slipway api\-resources
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Print the supported resource types with more information
slipway api\-resources \-o wide
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Print the names of the supported resource types
slipway api\-resources \-o name
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
